<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alhucemas landing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rif-war">Rif War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hoceima">Alhucemas</a> landing was an amphibious assault by Spanish forces, supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the bay of Alhucemas (Al Hoceima) in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> in September 1925. Landing close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-el-krim">Abd el-Krim</a>'s base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajdir">Ajdir</a>, the troops broke the Rifian resistance, and the Republic of the Rif surrendered in 1926. It is often regarded as the first modern combined air, sea and land landing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhucemas-landing.jpg" alt="Alhucemas landing" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Moreno Carbonero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desembarco_de_Alhucemas,_por_Jos%C3%A9_Moreno_Carbonero.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
